329 0 obj
<<
/Title (\(processing_system7_0\) connects, through an AXI Interconnect and a Processor System Reset block, to two AXI GPIO peripherals. The two switch inputs \(a_0, b_0\) are wired directly into the custom and_gate_v1_0 RTL IP, whose output c is captured by the first AXI GPIO \(axi_gpio_0\) as an input channel readable by software. The C application running on the PS reads this value, inverts it, and writes the result out through the second AXI GPIO \(axi_gpio_1\), whose output channel drives the external port gpio_io_o_0[0:0] connected to a user LED - completing the NAND function \(AND in hardware, NOT in software\). 4.1 Block Design)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 258 0 R
/Prev 328 0 R
>>
endobj
